    "updated_at": "2021-02-25T20:29:56Z",
    "body": "Ah, thanks! I got it to work with `starship config cmd_duration.show_notifications ...`. That seems like a reasonable first approach, although it seems to have two downsides:\r\n\r\n- the `starship config` command seems to destructively edit my `starship.toml`, e.g. it loses comments (cc https://github.com/alexcrichton/toml-rs/issues/214 / https://github.com/alexcrichton/toml-rs/issues/83 I guess) and removes my wrapping (with `\\`) from long strings\r\n- since it edits the global configuration, I think there's a few race conditions there, if there's multiple shells open (as I usually have):\r\n  - if another command legitimately finishes in the time between the `show_notifications` calls, it will incorrectly not show a notification\r\n  - if two `TRAPALRM` calls overlap, such that the `starship config cmd_duration.show_notifications true` of one happens right after `starship config cmd_duration.show_notifications false` of another, that second one will incorrectly reshow a notification\r\n\r\nHowever, I guess this suggests another more general approach: shell-local configuration, e.g. `STARSHIP_CONFIG_OVERRIDE='cmd_duration.show_notifications=false' starship_render` (which may tie into #565?).",
